        "description": "Identifies `gitsync sync` and `gitsync run` (without --dry-run), which force-push and prune every configured repo's branches and tags to GitHub so the two sides end up identical, and can eventually delete the GitHub mirror once a repo disappears from the source (subject to gitsync's own delete_grace and delete_limit safeguards).",
